  "implementation": [
    "A route origin captures only exact authenticated credential/Device/key metadata under the existing authentication lease and retains the existing authority lifetime registration. Actual delivery obtains one fresh peer/source read union; requests register their final signed wire ID before writing.",
    "A bounded live worker shares original source IDs across uncertainty and logical retry, deduplicates active source/target jobs, and releases other physical waiters when one decision commits. Waiting retains no application authority reader.",
    "The dedicated immutable source decision transaction uses fresh exact peer/source/membership/action/recipient and physical-current policy. It creates no ordinary operation/command, emits no invented ordinary operation correlation, and atomically commits the current Session change, journal and original decision. Storage failure rolls all of them back.",
    "The same configured host human-consent floor gates owned decisions. Identified observations cannot bypass it or invent a blocked command; actual consent and enrollment allow a new current physical waiter for the unchanged original source.",
    "receive_session_invitation and answer_session_invitation expose this native flow through the public Rust SDK. Directed invitations and other observations share one bounded inbox while keeping their receive APIs separate."
  ],
